      "id": 1,
      "text": "Nursery, Texas was founded in 1884 on land that once belonged to Silvestre De León.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nursery%2C_Texas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Horticulturist Gilbert Onderdonk opened a nursery there in 1883, giving the town its name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/nursery-tx-victoria-county",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A post office opened in 1884 with Onderdonk as postmaster, cementing Nursery’s early community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/nursery-tx-victoria-county",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The railroad made Nursery a convenient shipping point, thanks to its sandy loam soil with clay subsoil.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/nursery-tx-victoria-county",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "By 1900 the town boasted a train station, a doctor, a hotel, a gristmill, two cotton gins, and several stores.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/nursery-tx-victoria-county",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
